        ":question/problem": "Simplify.\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{10}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{10}\\right)}{\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{5}\\right)}\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Put $x=\\frac{\\pi}{10}$. Recall $2\\sin x\\cos x=\\sin(2x)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2\\sin x\\cos x}{\\cos(2x)} &=\\frac{2\\sin x\\cos x}{\\cos(2x)} \\\\ &=\\frac{\\sin(2x)}{\\cos(2x)} \\\\ &=\\tan(2x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe denominator is nonzero, and $\\tan(2x)=\\sin(2x)/\\cos(2x)$.\n\nSubstitute $x=\\frac{\\pi}{10}$ and double the whole angle: $2x=\\frac{\\pi}{5}$. The result is\n\n$$\n\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{5}\\right) .\n$$",
